lesson: 186
title: Balancing the scales
level: primary-4
stars: 2
explain: When the scales balance, both pans weigh the same. Take the same things off both pans and they still balance.
explain: Left: 5 cubes and 20 g. Right: 2 cubes and 110 g. Take 2 cubes and 20 g off each side: 3 cubes balance 90 g.
explain: So one cube weighs 90 ÷ 3 = 30 g.
vars: a=name c=10..60 p=3..8 q=2..6 u=10..100
need: q < p
let: v = u + c * (p - q)
need: v <= 400
answer: c
exercise: On the left pan of a balance there are {p} equal cubes and a weight of {u} g. On the right pan there are {q} such cubes and a weight of {v} g. The scales balance. How many grams does one cube weigh?
exercise: {a} puts {p} identical balls and a weight of {u} g on one pan, and {q} of the balls and a weight of {v} g on the other. The pans balance. How heavy is one ball in grams?
exercise: {p} equal jars and {u} g balance {q} of the same jars and {v} g. What is the weight of one jar in grams?
exercise: The scales are level with {p} equal blocks and {u} g on the left and {q} equal blocks and {v} g on the right. How many grams is one block?
exercise: {a} balances {p} equal apples and a weight of {u} g against {q} equal apples and a weight of {v} g. How much does one apple weigh in grams?
test: A weight of {v} g together with {q} identical toy cars weighs exactly as much as {p} of the cars together with a weight of {u} g. Find the weight of one car in grams.
test: {a}'s balance is level: one side holds a weight of {u} g and {p} equal soaps, the other side {q} equal soaps and {v} g of weights. How many grams does a single soap weigh?
test: How many grams does each cube weigh, if {q} cubes and {v} g on one side of a balance weigh as much as {p} cubes and {u} g on the other?
exercise: How many grams does one cube weigh if {p} equal cubes and {u} g on the left pan balance {q} such cubes and {v} g on the right pan?
exercise: {a} in Ohio balances {p} identical marbles and a weight of {u} g against {q} of the marbles and a weight of {v} g. What is the mass of one marble in grams?
exercise: Left pan: {p} equal cubes and {u} g. Right pan: {q} equal cubes and {v} g. The pans balance. How many grams is one cube?
exercise: On a kitchen scale in Leeds, {p} equal eggs and a weight of {u} g balance {q} equal eggs and a weight of {v} g. How many grams does each egg weigh?
exercise: A shopkeeper in Toronto puts {p} identical bars of soap and {u} g of weights on one side, and {q} of the same bars with {v} g of weights on the other. The two sides balance. How heavy is each bar in grams?
exercise: {a} has a toy balance in Sydney. {q} equal wooden blocks and {v} g on one pan weigh as much as {p} equal blocks and {u} g on the other. Find the weight of one block in grams.
exercise: {p} identical potatoes plus {u} g weigh the same as {q} identical potatoes plus {v} g. How many grams does each potato weigh?
exercise: In a science class in Dublin the scales are level when the left pan has {p} equal metal nuts and {u} g, and the right pan has {q} such nuts and {v} g. What does one nut weigh in grams?
test: A bag of {u} g and {p} same-sized plums weigh exactly as much as a bag of {v} g and {q} of those plums. In grams, how heavy is one plum?
test: The two pans are even: {v} g and {q} identical tins on the right, {u} g and {p} identical tins on the left. How many grams does a tin weigh?
test: All of {a}'s toy trains in Texas weigh the same. {p} trains plus {u} g balance {q} trains plus {v} g. What is the weight of one train in grams?
test: A jeweller in Auckland finds that {q} equal beads with {v} g of weights balance {p} equal beads with {u} g. How many grams does a single bead weigh?
test: What is the weight in grams of one chocolate bar, if {p} equal bars and {u} g on a scale weigh as much as {q} equal bars and {v} g?
test: {a} puts {u} g and {p} equal coins in the left pan; to balance them, {a.he} needs {q} of the same coins and {v} g in the right pan. Find the weight of one coin in grams.
exercise: left pan {p} same cubes + {u} g weight, right pan {q} cubes + {v} g. balances. how heavy one cube in g
exercise: {a} put {p} same balls n a {u} g weight on one side, {q} balls n {v} g on the other, it balances. 1 ball's how many g
exercise: {p} cubes + {u} g one side, {q} cubes + {v+10} — no wait, {v} g other side. level. grams per cube
exercise: scales at school (the old ones from like 1990), {p} same apples + {u} g left, {q} apples + {v} g right, even. how many g one apple
test: Sam just added {u} and {v}. nah. {p} equal cubes n {u} g vs {q} cubes n {v} g, balanced, how heavy one cube
test: {q} same blocks + {v} g on the right, {p} blocks + {u} g on the left, scales level. one block in grams
test: {a}'s balancing {p} identical toy cars plus {u} g against {q} of em plus {v} g. even. how many g per car
exam: Upon the left pan of a balance are placed {p} cubes of equal mass together with a weight of {u} grams; upon the right pan are placed {q} such cubes together with a weight of {v} grams. Given that the balance is in equilibrium, determine the mass of one cube in grams.
exam: It is given that {p} identical balls and a weight of {u} g placed upon one pan exactly counterbalance {q} of the said balls and a weight of {v} g placed upon the other. Ascertain the mass, in grams, of a single ball.
exam: Whereas a balance is found to be in equilibrium when one pan bears {p} equal bricks and {u} grams and the other bears {q} equal bricks and {v} grams, state the mass of one brick expressed in grams.
exam: Determine, in grams, the mass of each of a number of identical tins, given that {p} tins with a weight of {u} grams are in equilibrium upon a balance with {q} tins and a weight of {v} grams.
exercise: {a} had {p+q+1} equal cubes, but {a.his} little brother 'liberated' one. {a} puts {p} of the rest and a {u} g weight on one pan, and all the others with a {v} g weight on the other. The pans balance. How many grams does one cube weigh?
exercise: Grandad passed away and left {a} his old scales and {p+q} identical brass cubes. {a} puts {p} of them with a {u} g weight on the left pan, and the rest with a {v} g weight on the right. It balances. How heavy is one cube in grams?
test: crap, the dog ate one, rest in peace. so {p} cubes + {u} g on the left now, {q} cubes + {v} g on the right, level. one cube in g? don't be thick
